# Multi-User Games — VTC

Use when building or integrating a game under `~/games/` with **LobbyNet** (global dedicated lobby) matchmaking and shared realtime.

Related: `realtime.mdc` (ws.vtc.com + JWT), `auth-bootstrap.mdc` (URL `?token=`).

## Architecture (three pieces)

| Piece | Repo | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| **Lobby hub** | `~/games/lobbynet` | Global matchmaking (db_1_2), player list, start game, SSE + Socket.IO |
| **Game app** | `~/games/{chess, poker, ...}` | Game logic, state, `/api/game-info`, `/lobby-start` |
| **Realtime relay** | `wss://ws.vtc.com` | Room pub/sub — **not** chat.vtc.com |

Games are **not** pre-registered. Lobby discovers a game when the user arrives with `?gameUrl={GAME_URL}&token={JWT}`.

## Required env vars (game app)

Add to `env_development` and `.env.production` — never hardcode URLs.

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` | This game's public URL (used as `gameUrl`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_LOBBY_URL` | LobbyNet URL (prod: `https://lobbynet.apps.vtc.com`; dev: `http://127.0.0.1:3012`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL` | `https://ws.vtc.com` (shared relay; JWT required) |

LobbyNet also needs `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL`, Redis (`REDIS_*`), and lobby port (`3012` typical).

## Integration contract (game app)

### 1. Entry — redirect authenticated users to lobby

On home / create-game flow, when JWT exists:

```
{NEXT_PUBLIC_LOBBY_URL}?gameUrl={encodeURIComponent(NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL)}&token={jwt}
```

Reference: `~/games/chess/app/page.tsx`

### 2. `GET /api/game-info`

Lobby fetches this to show name, limits, metadata fields. Enable CORS (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`).

**Required fields:**

```json
{
  "id": "chess",
  "name": "Chess",
  "minPlayers": 2,
  "maxPlayers": 2
}
```

- `id` — stable slug; written to LobbyNet `game_registry` when present
- `gameType` — optional alias of `id` for plugins
- `metadataFields` — optional lobby form fields (select, number, etc.)

Reference: `~/games/chess/app/api/game-info/route.ts`

### 3. `/lobby-start` page

Lobby redirects here when host starts:

```
{gameServerUrl}/lobby-start?lobbyId=...&players=...&metadata=...
```

- Parse `lobbyId`, player list, metadata
- **Use `lobbyId` as the game session ID** (Redis key, Mongo id, URL segment)
- Create game state, redirect players into the match

Reference: `~/games/chess/app/lobby-start/` (or equivalent route)

### 4. Re-join / spectate

Support URLs like `/game/{lobbyId}` so players can return via lobby links.

### 5. Realtime — Socket.IO on ws.vtc.com

- **Room id = `lobbyId`** (plain string): `socket.emit('join-room', lobbyId)`
- **JWT on connect** — from URL `?token=` → localStorage → `auth: { token }` on client
- **Server-side broadcasts** — pass JWT from request into socket client (`getTokenFromRequest`)
- Dev: connect to `https://ws.vtc.com` with VTC dev launcher token — **no** local ws Docker, **no** `dev-secret` fallback

Reference: `~/games/chess/lib/websocket.ts`, `lib/socketio-server.ts`, `~/games/lobbynet/src/lib/socketio-client.ts`

Read `realtime.mdc` before adding socket code.

## LobbyNet hub (only when changing the lobby app)

- Game plugins: `~/games/lobbynet/src/lib/game-plugins/`
- Auto-register: `GET {gameUrl}/api/game-info` on lobby load (`LayoutContent` / registry)
- Start flow: redirect to `lobby.gameServerUrl/lobby-start?...`
- Do **not** hardcode per-game URLs — use `gameServerUrl` from the lobby object

## Standalone vs lobby-integrated

| Mode | Needs |
|------|-------|
| Standalone (no lobby) | Normal VTC child app + optional `realtime.mdc` only |
| Lobby multiplayer | Full contract above |

Do not add lobby redirects or `/api/game-info` unless the game should appear in LobbyNet.

## AI checklist (new lobby game)

1. Confirm game lives under `~/games/` and has `.cursor` linked to `~/games/cursor`
2. Add env vars: `NEXT_PUBLIC_LOBBY_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`
3. Implement `GET /api/game-info` with `id`, `minPlayers`, `maxPlayers`
4. Redirect home → lobby with `gameUrl` + `token`
5. Implement `/lobby-start` — `lobbyId` = session id
6. Socket.IO: `join-room` with `lobbyId`, JWT on client and server emits
7. Copy auth pattern from chess: `getTokenFromRequest`, no env JWT fallback
8. Test: launch from VTC dev section → lobby → create → start → both players in same room

## Reference implementations

| What | Where |
|------|-------|
| Full game integration | `~/games/chess` |
| Lobby hub | `~/games/lobbynet` |
| Chess plugin (metadata) | `~/games/lobbynet/src/lib/game-plugins/chess-integration.ts` |

## Do not

- Hardcode game URLs in LobbyNet (use dynamic `gameServerUrl`)
- Use `chat.vtc.com` for game moves or lobby updates
- Skip `id` in `game-info` if registry / leaderboards matter
- Add `DEV_JWT_TOKEN` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_JWT_TOKEN` env fallbacks — token comes from VTC shell `?token=` only
